  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** CVRx’s Barostim therapy is entering a period of gathering commercial momentum, helped by the January 2026 shift to Category I CPT codes, which is already reducing prior-authorization friction and improving Medicare Advantage approval rates. Revenue growth is accelerating, supported by a maturing base of active implanting centres. The key structural catalyst is the recently initiated BENEFIT‑HF randomised trial, which aims to expand the addressable patient population more than twofold and dramatically enlarge the total market opportunity, bolting a long-term growth path onto the current commercial business.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership has prudently strengthened the balance sheet by extending debt maturities and securing additional capital to cover the BENEFIT‑HF trial’s multi‑year cash cost. The commercial organisation has been refocused on higher‑potential accounts after building out U.S. territories, while the rapid activation of trial sites and early first‑patient enrollment signal disciplined clinical execution. Forward guidance suggests a steady, measured ramp, and the early 2026 reimbursement data indicate management’s market‑access efforts are translating into tangible operational gains.",
